.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause
.Dd September 6, 2026
.Dt AETHER-USERLAND-QUALITY 1
.Os Aether-userland experimental
.Sh NAME
.Nm aether-userland-quality
.Nd check local standards integrity and documentation inventory
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm python3
.Fl B
.Pa docs/quality/check.py
.Op Fl h | Fl -help
.Op Fl -version
.Op Fl -release
.Sh DESCRIPTION
This page describes the existing quality 0.1.0 contributor checker.
The manual name is a lookup label, not an installed executable.
Run the command from the Aether-userland checkout root.
The declared interpreter requirement is Python 3.10 or later;
validation records identify the interpreter actually tested.
No native Aether Python runtime or target installation is implied.
.Pp
With no options, the checker verifies the approved-draft manifest pin
and its complete file inventory before loading its validator.
It runs the private integrity controls, checks the pinned Foundations,
Distribution and Experience copies, then validates the local documentation
inventory structure and referenced file paths.
The repository root is derived from the checker file location.
.Pp
A successful check establishes only the named integrity and structural results.
It does not establish source authenticity, complete documentation,
independent review, native execution, POSIX conformance or release authorization.
Reference checkers execute trusted local Python code after byte verification.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print usage and available options to standard output and exit successfully
without checking the standards inputs.
.It Fl -version
Print
.Dq quality 0.1.0
to standard output and exit successfully without checking the standards inputs.
.It Fl -release
Also require complete documentation inventory entries.
Draft or blocked entries prevent success.
Even a successful preflight would not authorize publication.
This checkout currently rejects incomplete release coverage.
.El
.Pp
There are no positional operands.
Unknown options and extra operands are usage errors.
The current Python argument parser accepts unambiguous long-option prefixes
and repeated boolean options; use full option names in scripts.
Help and version stop parsing when encountered.
No quiet, color, progress, JSON or automatic pin-update option is provided.
.Sh OUTPUT
Check reports use standard output.
Usage errors and caught operational failures use standard error.
Child checks can also write diagnostics and test summaries to standard error
even when the overall check succeeds.
Child streams are retained separately and replayed after cleanup.
Each output file has a 16 MiB limit.
There is no promised ordering between different output streams.
The checker adds no color or animation.
Treat prose reports as human diagnostics, not a stable machine schema.
Preserve the distinct runtime
.Dq NOT RUN
report when recording a successful structural check.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
The parent uses the invoking Python environment.
Reference children use the same absolute interpreter with
.Fl B ,
a fixed
.Ev PATH
of /usr/bin:/bin,
.Ev LC_ALL=C ,
and a private
.Ev TMPDIR
under the checkout build directory.
Other parent environment variables are not copied to these children.
Use
.Fl B
as shown to suppress bytecode output in the parent as well.
Use a trusted interpreter, checkout and environment.
There is no dedicated environment variable for choosing a different standards pin.
No network provisioning or target installation is performed by this workflow.
.Sh FILES
All paths below are relative to the checkout root.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa build/quality-process-*
Private retained child input, output and process receipts.
No automatic pruning is performed.
.It Pa docs/quality/simplicity.sha256
Manifest digest for the separately adopted unreleased simplicity extension.
.It Pa docs/vendor/aether-review-snapshots/2026-09-07/coding-v0.2.0
Offline additive simplicity snapshot; released pins remain unchanged.
.It Pa docs/quality/drafts.sha256
Approved-draft manifest identity.
.It Pa docs/vendor/aether-approved-drafts/2026-09-05
Offline approved draft snapshot, not a published replacement release.
.It Pa docs/quality/coverage.json
Documentation surface inventory; draft entries remain incomplete.
.It Pa docs/standards.lock
Foundations release pin.
.It Pa docs/distribution.lock
Distribution release pin.
.It Pa docs/experience.lock
Experience release pin.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It 0
The selected checks passed, or help/version was printed.
.It 1
A caught integrity, inventory, file or child-check failure occurred.
Incomplete release coverage also returns 1.
.It 64
Invalid command-line usage.
.El
.Pp
An interruption, interpreter startup failure or uncaught exception is not a
successful check and may have a platform-specific outcome.
The program does not provide a total in-process validation deadline.
Its integrity-control child has a 30-second timeout and each of the three
reference-check children has a 60-second timeout.
Each child runs in an owned session.
Timeout or descendants remaining after leader exit trigger group cleanup
and a failed check.
Cleanup has a bounded additional wait; unresolved cleanup cannot pass.
Children that deliberately detach from the session and uncatchable owner
termination are outside this trusted-checker cleanup contract.
.Sh EXAMPLES
No root authority is required.
From the checkout root, inspect the command without running its checks:
.Bd -literal
python3 -B docs/quality/check.py --help
python3 -B docs/quality/check.py --version
.Ed
.Pp
Both commands return 0; the second prints
.Dq quality 0.1.0 .
Run the local gate:
.Bd -literal
python3 -B docs/quality/check.py
.Ed
.Pp
Expect status 0 only when the pins and inventory pass, with a separate
report that runtime and publication gates were not run.
Check publication completeness:
.Bd -literal
python3 -B docs/quality/check.py --release
.Ed
.Pp
The current experimental inventory returns 1 with
.Dq FAILED: incomplete release entry .
This is an open documentation gate, not permission to remove draft entries.
.Sh DIAGNOSTICS
A pin or content mismatch requires investigation of the changed bytes.
Compare the retained manifest, source and review evidence before restoring
an authorized input or proposing an explicit new adoption.
Never regenerate a pin merely to silence a mismatch.
.Pp
For an incomplete release entry, finish the named surface's documentation,
exact revision, evidence and required reviews.
Consult
.Pa docs/quality/PROCESS.md
and
.Pa .planning/BACKLOG.md
for the UL-061 through UL-063 migration work.
For a child failure, retain both output streams and the actual exit status;
do not report a timeout or missing tool as semantic rejection.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Pa CONTRIBUTING.md ,
.Pa docs/quality/PROCESS.md ,
.Pa docs/quality/RC1-ADP02.md ,
.Pa docs/quality/coverage.json
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Aether contributors
.Sh SECURITY CONSIDERATIONS
A checksum identifies bytes, not publisher authority or runtime confinement.
The checker executes verified local reference code and does not sandbox it.
The process helper accounts for non-detached descendants of trusted checks;
it is not a sandbox for hostile code.
Do not run checks from an unreviewed checkout with elevated authority.
